# Proposed real-world workflow


**Step 1**

Vineyard employee would photograph grapevine leaves furing routine field monitoring

OR

Photographs of leaves are automatically taken by in-situ cameras.

**Step 2**

CNN analyses each photograph and returns proabilities for each disease. These predictions are used as a triage signal.

**Step 3**

Agronomist prioritizes review of leaves highlighted by the model as diseased. Expert takes into account the result but also does a visual inspection in-situ before deciding which step to take next.

**Step 4**

Monitor/ sampling/ treatment as agronomist sees fit.

